.\" Manpage for escp.
.\" Contact solutions@agilemindswork.uk to fix typos.
.TH ESCP 1 "May 2026" "escp 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
escp \- emit Epson ESC/P and ESC/P 2 printer control sequences
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B escp
.RI [ OPTIONS .\|.\|.]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B escp
writes Epson \fBESC/P\fR and \fBESC/P 2\fR control sequences to standard
output, or to a file given with
.BR -o .
Each option is processed left-to-right, so the order of the resulting
byte stream matches the order of the options on the command line.
.PP
The tool is intended for use in shell pipelines that turn plain text
into a print-ready stream for an Epson-compatible 9- or 24-pin
dot-matrix printer.  It was designed for the
.B PSI PP-404
in EPSON LQ 2550 emulation but works with any printer that speaks the
standard Epson command set.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS General
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output \fIFILE\fR
Write the output bytes to \fIFILE\fR instead of standard output.
.TP
.B \-i, \-\-init, \-\-reset
Emit \fBESC @\fR (1B 40) to initialise the printer.  Recommended as the
first option in every invocation.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print the program version and exit.
.SS Single-byte control codes
.TP
.B \-\-bs \-\-ht \-\-lf \-\-vt \-\-ff \-\-cr \-\-del \-\-cancel
Emit the corresponding ASCII control byte (BS, HT, LF, VT, FF, CR, DEL,
CAN).
.TP
.B \-\-select  \-\-deselect
Emit DC1 (11h) or DC3 (13h) to bring the printer on- or off-line.
.TP
.B \-\-condensed  \-\-cancel\-condensed
Emit SI (0Fh) or DC2 (12h).
.TP
.B \-\-double\-width\-line  \-\-cancel\-double\-width\-line
Emit SO (0Eh) or DC4 (14h) for one-line double-width.
.SS Printer state
.TP
.B \-\-msb\-0, \-\-msb\-1, \-\-msb\-cancel
Control the most-significant bit of subsequent data (\fBESC =\fR,
\fBESC >\fR, \fBESC #\fR).
.SS Pitch and font
.TP
.B \-\-pica, \-\-elite
Select 10 cpi (\fBESC P\fR) or 12 cpi (\fBESC M\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-cpi \fIN\fR
Shortcut for one of \-\-pica, \-\-elite or \fBESC g\fR (15 cpi).
\fIN\fR must be 10, 12 or 15.
.TP
.B \-\-proportional \fRon|off
Cancel or select proportional spacing (\fBESC p\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-font \fINAME\fR
Select a font family by name.  Accepts: \fIroman\fR, \fIsans\fR
(Letter Gothic), \fIcourier\fR, \fIprestige\fR, \fIscript\fR, \fIocr-a\fR,
\fIocr-b\fR, \fIorator\fR, \fIorator-c\fR, \fIdata-block\fR,
\fIdata-large\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-quality \fRdraft|lq
Select draft or letter-quality printing (\fBESC x\fR).
.SS Style attributes
.TP
.B \-\-bold \fRon|off
Select or cancel emphasised printing (\fBESC E\fR / \fBESC F\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-double\-strike \fRon|off
Select or cancel double-strike (\fBESC G\fR / \fBESC H\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-italic \fRon|off
Italics on or off (\fBESC 4\fR / \fBESC 5\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-underline \fRon|off
Underline on or off (\fBESC -\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-script \fRsuper|sub|none
Superscript, subscript or cancel (\fBESC S\fR / \fBESC T\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-double\-width \fRon|off
Multi-line double width (\fBESC W\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-double\-height \fRon|off
Double-height printing (\fBESC w\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-style \fRnormal|outline|shadow|outline-shadow
Character style (\fBESC q\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-master \fIN\fR
Send the raw master-select bit-mask \fIN\fR (0\-255) via \fBESC !\fR.
The individual bits select pitch and style according to Appendix F
Table 5 of the printer manual.
.SS Layout
.TP
.B \-\-line\-spacing \fR1/6|1/8
Set the line spacing to 1/6\(dq (\fBESC 2\fR) or 1/8\(dq (\fBESC 0\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-line\-spacing\-60 \fIN\fR
Set line spacing to \fIN\fR/60\(dq (\fBESC A\fR; 0\(en127).
.TP
.B \-\-line\-spacing\-180 \fIN\fR
Set line spacing to \fIN\fR/180\(dq (\fBESC 3\fR; 0\(en255).
.TP
.B \-\-line\-spacing\-360 \fIN\fR
Set line spacing to \fIN\fR/360\(dq (\fBESC +\fR; 0\(en255).
.TP
.B \-\-feed\-180 \fIN\fR, \-\-reverse\-feed\-180 \fIN\fR
Perform a forward (\fBESC J\fR) or reverse (\fBESC j\fR) line feed of
\fIN\fR/180\(dq.
.TP
.B \-\-page\-lines \fIN\fR
Set the form length to \fIN\fR lines (\fBESC C\fR; 1\(en127).
.TP
.B \-\-page\-inches \fIN\fR
Set the form length to \fIN\fR inches (\fBESC C NUL\fR; 1\(en22).
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-perf \fIN\fR, \-\-no\-skip\-perf
Set or clear the skip-over-perforation distance (\fBESC N\fR / \fBESC O\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-left\-margin \fIN\fR, \-\-right\-margin \fIN\fR
Set the left (\fBESC l\fR) and right (\fBESC Q\fR) margins, in columns
of the current pitch.
.TP
.B \-\-lpi \fIN\fR
Convenience option: 6 \(-> \fBESC 2\fR, 8 \(-> \fBESC 0\fR, otherwise
\fBESC 3\fR with the calculated /180\(dq parameter.
.SS Print position
.TP
.B \-\-h\-pos \fIN\fR
Set the absolute horizontal print position to \fIN\fR/60\(dq from the
left margin (\fBESC $\fR; \fIN\fR 0\(en65535).  The value is sent
little-endian (low byte first).
.TP
.B \-\-h\-rel \fIN\fR
Move the print head by \fIN\fR units relative to the current position
(\fBESC \\\fR; signed 16-bit).
.TP
.B \-\-v\-pos \fIN\fR, \-\-v\-rel \fIN\fR
ESC/P 2 absolute and relative vertical positioning (\fBESC ( V\fR and
\fBESC ( v\fR).
.SS Character set
.TP
.B \-\-upper\-print, \-\-upper\-control
Treat code points 128\(en159 as printable characters
(\fBESC 6\fR) or as control codes (\fBESC 7\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-country \fIN\fR
Select the national character set \fIN\fR (\fBESC R\fR; 0\(en15).
.TP
.B \-\-charset \fIN\fR
Select character table \fIN\fR (\fBESC t\fR; 0\(en3).
.SS Tabs and direction
.TP
.B \-\-clear\-htabs, \-\-clear\-vtabs
Clear all horizontal or vertical tab stops.
.TP
.B \-\-unidirectional \fRon|off, \-\-uni\-line
Force unidirectional printing.  \fB\-\-uni\-line\fR applies to one line
only (\fBESC <\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-justify \fRleft|center|right|full
Set the text justification (\fBESC a\fR).
.SS Inline data
.TP
.B \-\-text \fISTRING\fR
Emit \fISTRING\fR verbatim.
.TP
.B \-\-raw \fIHEX\fR
Emit the bytes encoded in \fIHEX\fR.  Spaces, commas, colons and
\fB0x\fR prefixes are ignored, so all of \fB1b40\fR, \fB1B 40\fR and
\fB0x1B,0x40\fR are equivalent.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B escp
exits 0 on success and 2 if a command-line argument is invalid, an
output file cannot be opened, or a write fails.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Reset, print a bold header, body text, then form-feed:
.PP
.RS
.nf
{
    escp --init --cpi 12
    escp --bold on --text "INVOICE 0042" --bold off --lf --lf
    cat invoice.txt
    escp --ff
} > /dev/lp0
.fi
.RE
.PP
Send arbitrary bytes (for example, the PP-404 eject-form sequence):
.PP
.RS
.nf
escp --raw "1B 5B 3C 73"
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/escp
The installed binary.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/man/man1/escp.1
This manual page.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lp (1),
.BR lpr (1),
.BR cat (1)
.PP
EPSON ESC/P Reference Manual (Seiko Epson Corp., 1997).
.PP
PSI PP-404 Operator's Manual, Appendix F.
.SH BUGS
Bit-image graphics commands (\fBESC K\fR, \fBESC L\fR, \fBESC Y\fR,
\fBESC Z\fR, \fBESC *\fR), user-defined characters (\fBESC &\fR),
macro definition and bar-code printing are not mapped to dedicated
options.  Emit them with \fB\-\-raw\fR if you need them.
